WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Athena, a fantasy world of boundless adventure awaits you.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:26.920
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.600
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:35.900
And I'm Joe. Guys, today we're playing Athena, the Greek goddess, but here just a princess, I think.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.280
Well, she... Yes.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.840
Yeah, you're right. She is just a princess.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.080
In this game, yes.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.560
Don't reduce the action of religion.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.100
Don't be like, yo, but she's always just been a princess.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.600
I mean, but it is interesting to see like a hero princess.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.640
And they do call her the goddess of wisdom.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.280
I think they're still like trying to pretend that it's the same person, but it's not.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.040
But this, yeah, maybe it was her when she was younger.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.040
Maybe, yeah. It's her origin story.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.600
This is her origin story.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.560
And yeah, Sean, I think you were trying to get the fact that maybe this is like our

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.000
first female character.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.040
Yeah. Clu-Clu-Land.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.860
Okay. But that's a humanoid.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.020
That's a female like blob.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.520
We had that debate about Mock Rider, remember?

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.740
Because there's that one screen where like Mock Rider takes off the outfit and it's like

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.920
this, you know, chick.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.320
Yeah. Chick. Okay.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.560
Like, I didn't want to say girl because she's like, all right, she's a woman.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.220
She's a woman. But like the thing was, it's like we weren't, you know, she's not even in the same pose.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.120
We're not sure if they were insinuating this is who Mock Rider was.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.160
Because you are Mock Rider.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.040
Right. That's right. But we also didn't see anybody else in that world.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.040
Yeah. So we could just assume that that also could be Mock Rider because people don't exist anymore.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.320
It's just you and the.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.880
Like cars. Like you're the last human before cars.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.620
And the buggies and all that.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.800
So that's a prequel to cars.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.780
This is a prequel to Greek mythology.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.480
Yeah. This is like, which came first, Kid Icarus or this?

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.220
Oh, yeah. That's a good point.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.460
You know, because chronologically, Kid Icarus came first.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.520
We already did that episode.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.800
But now we're here with Athena.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.200
So, okay. Yeah.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.520
It is our first, at least, adventure game where you know that this is a

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.400
female character the entire time that we're playing.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.480
Right. Yeah. That's fine.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.560
I feel like it's a big deal. Yeah.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:27.200
Even though she's not the best dressed character to represent a woman in a video game on the NES.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.440
It's a little, it's stupid.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.220
Like why, I mean like apparently you're just going to walk around.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.240
I mean it's 8-bit graphics so you can't really, it doesn't really look like anything.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.100
Yeah. She's wearing a red bikini.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.300
At least on like one of the covers.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.920
One version of the cover.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.260
It's a red bikini. I couldn't even tell while playing the game because I hadn't looked at the box art.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.720
The part that bothers me though is how they explain it.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.500
And if you, you have to play the arcade version to really understand it.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.840
For those, for those cinematics, right?

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:09.740
For the cinematics of like, well the reason why she has all of her clothes off at the start of the game is because she opened a door to that fantasy world and then she falls down and as she's falling all of her clothes came off.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.980
Yeah. But why, that doesn't explain why that happened.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:22.380
And if you're thinking, well okay guys, we can grant them all of that but it's still a pretty progressive move to, no.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:28.480
It's not because the only reason that she opened the door to chaos was because she was bored.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:32.200
And it's like, that's just what they think that women do, isn't it?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:38.080
Like, the only times that like, they have to be heroic is when they're, like when they're bored and they do some stupid shit on their own, right?

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.360
So, uh. They cause the problem, you know what I'm saying?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.260
I feel like, you know, I'd be, I wouldn't, you know, having this information I need to dish it out.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:51.780
We have, uh, Toshiyuki Nakai, uh, which was a complete, that's not his name at all probably, knowing me.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.880
Uh, but let's go, let's just call him Toshi.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.000
Uh, he was the designer and planner for Athena.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.240
And, um, Athena wound up being a pretty popular character for SNK.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.340
Uh, and so he answers a couple questions about it in a 1996 interview.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:12.920
And on the design of Athena, he doesn't talk anything about the red bikini and instead just says,

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.340
Developing Athena was an unforgettable experience for me.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.960
I drew Athena herself and most of the other characters.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.200
So besides its popularity, it left a big impression on me.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:31.940
And then follows it up with, we also received a bunch of fan letters sent directly to Athena, the game character herself.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.640
And lots of postcards with illustrations on them.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:38.100
It probably doesn't seem rare at all today, but back then it was very new.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.680
And I remember everyone at SNK was surprised.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.420
Dear Athena, would you like to go to prom with me?

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:49.060
Right. As her character designer, it was a huge encouragement to me and made me very happy.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.140
In an instant, all the exhaustion and pain I felt dissipated.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:54.960
All right. Yeah.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.980
So, I mean, he's proud of the work he did.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.040
Good for him. Even though Sean seems to have some beef with Toji Yuki over here.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:06.360
I have no beef. I just think it's funny that it, like, she opened, like, that is such an origin story.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.740
Is that bored thing in the story in the manual?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.120
I'm sorry, what? Is the bored aspect of it?

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.580
Yes, it is in the manual.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:21.020
She was bored. Okay, so just to take a step back for a minute, as I mentioned about Toji Yuki, this is an SNK game.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.900
This is their second NES game.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.740
Their first was Ikari Warriors.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.580
Can we talk a little bit about Ikari Warriors for a second?

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.760
How do we feel about that game?

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:38.420
Do you have high hopes for Athena because of Ikari Warriors, or are you expecting, like, something mediocre?

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:44.920
I'd say I was expecting not—I was not expecting the world from this game, and it still did not reach that bar.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.480
Gotcha. I also wasn't expecting much, but I was expecting more than I got.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.200
And so Micronix did the NES port.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:58.060
SNK hasn't done either of those games, Ikari Warriors or Athena.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.040
They just did the arcade versions.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.540
But Micronix does the NES port, and Micronix did Ghost and Goblins in 1942.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.980
Those are Capcom games.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.240
But it also did Ikari Warriors.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:17.840
So it's kind of like, you know, you don't—I feel like all three of those games are recognizable even today, like, to a retro gamer enthusiast.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:23.100
So Micronix is doing a good job here in terms of making memorable games, but are they making good games?

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:31.940
I mean, the game itself doesn't seem like it was that well-programmed.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:42.780
Like, there's a lot of actual jank in this game where—like, one thing that I noticed and that I read and just, like, watched videos about,

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:50.840
there is no—there is no, like, buffer between when you get hit and when you can get hit again.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:56.360
Like, if you just end up in a crowd of enemies, you will just die in a second.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:01.400
Because every frame that you intersect with one of them is damage.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:11.200
Wow. Yeah, so if there's, like, those horse guys coming at you from both sides, you could just be, like, kind of squeezed into a position where you're just going to take a ton of damage.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:19.600
Yes. And there are other things with, like, hitboxes not working, and you can just get locked out of the game if you don't have an item on you.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:20.660
I got trapped. Yeah.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:21.920
I got trapped on the first level.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.160
The very first level.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:31.480
There's a guy firing arrows with, like, a rapid-fire bow and arrow, and I went—there's two levels.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.720
You can go down or you can go up, and I went down, and at that point, the arrows were just coming in behind me.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:40.260
They didn't reach me, but they completely blocked me from going the only way back out.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.600
Huh. So I had to take a death.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.220
They were going too fast.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.520
There was no possible way of avoiding them.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.660
Yeah, I didn't think the game would softlock you.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.640
Yeah. No, it does a lot.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:56.780
Wow. Okay. I didn't experience that during my playthrough, but I guess it makes sense because I was kind of just pushing through at all times,

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:02.420
so I didn't really, like, take a moment to, like, let anything happen in the world that I was experiencing.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.120
I just kind of kept moving forward.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:12.700
Yeah. But also, if you end up in a boss battle with the wrong weapon, you can just not be able to do any actual damage.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:15.880
Oh, yeah, and that's a big problem in the final boss, which we'll talk about later.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:20.920
But let's just go into the plot beats for a minute here with Athena since there is a plot.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:31.320
She was the princess of the heavenly kingdom of victory, and one day she opened the door which shouldn't be opened in the basement of Castle Victory.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:42.040
And when she crossed into the doorway, it caused her to fall from the skies into another realm called Fantasy World, which was dominated by the evil emperor Dante.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:49.000
After her flowing dress was lost while catching the wind for her fall, the game begins in the world of forest.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.160
So I don't know a ton about Greek mythology.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:54.320
But that doesn't sound like any of it.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.680
And that doesn't, yeah, that doesn't ring familiar.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:04.700
It is weird that they even chose to, you know, talk about the Greek thing at all, considering that, like, even the enemies in the game.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.980
There's zero actual Greek influence.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:08.300
It's just the name of the character.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.220
Right. Guys, how influenced are you after playing, like, Kid Icarus?

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:23.360
Like, how influenced are you to not give this game a pass because you just had, like, a game that, like, was able to be fun and kind of modern while also having those same kind of, like, fun references at Greek mythology?

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.880
I don't think I would be willing to give this game a pass anyways.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:34.300
But, yeah, that is just, like, just further, like, solidifies my thought of, like, this game did it right before you.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.520
It did it right and it did it first.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:41.120
And, like, it's not like there's a right and a wrong way, but it's, like, it feels like Kid Icarus kind of did its homework.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:44.220
Well, again, I don't think that that's what they were going for.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.900
Just remove the name Athena.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:49.220
Sure. And just call her Bathina.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:53.440
And, I mean, it doesn't make any other allusions.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.500
It's not out of place.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:55.580
I guess that's true.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:01.360
But it does say in the manual Athena, goddess of wisdom, which I guess could be a different Athena, a different goddess of wisdom, and a different religion.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:04.340
But it leads me on to believe that there's –

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:06.880
I'm excited because I know I'm going to open a whole can of worms later.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.640
So I'm very excited for when I open them.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.680
And let's talk about the gameplay.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:45.520
Either one of you guys want to, like, walk me through just, like, kind of what you do in this game?

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.540
I would like to hear what Sean has to say.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:51.960
Sean? I feel like you maybe experienced it more.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:11:00.680
Let me hear it, Sean. So you start off just – it's a typical side-scrolling action game.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:16.900
But you – and you have to find armor and weapons by either stealing weapons from downed enemies or digging into the dirt to find either helmet, boots, shield.

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:19.360
Do you actually get, like, chest armor?

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.700
I don't know. Yeah, you do. You do have – yeah, there's a couple different – like, you get the helmet, the chest armor.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:27.240
I think you can even get, like – is there boots or something, I think?

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.280
Yeah, boots. Yeah. Yeah, I mentioned that.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:34.560
And they all have different, like, defensive bonuses and movement bonuses.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:43.100
Like, if you have the helmet, you can jump into a block, and it'll break the block, which will give you some sort of pickup.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:58.960
But basically the entire game is trying to build your armor set and getting the best weapons for the situation and progressing through the game to the right or in some of the later levels into some, like, labyrinthine.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.080
I mean, it's not that complicated.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:07.320
Yeah, I'm kind of inclined – you know, like, my immediate thought was, like, oh, is this one of those, like, Super Mario Brothers clones?

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.260
And I don't think so.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:14.280
I think it's more like a chubby cherub, you know, like, on a similar scale.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.660
I guess. That's a comparative game that we've talked about in the past.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:21.640
I think that's the one that, like, rings most true to what's going on in Athena.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:33.260
Yeah. I guess that both of those games do this thing that we've mentioned before, too, where it feels like the enemy placement and just the design of the level is just kind of –

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:35.440
There is no enemy placement. There's not a lot of thought put behind it.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.980
It's just like, let's just put things wherever that can hit you, and it doesn't feel –

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:57.460
Yeah, this is the same, like, whatever technique a lot of these games have been using of just, like, endlessly spawning, almost randomly spawning, infinitely spawning enemies of varying types that it can actually get to a point where you just can't progress because there's just a crowd of horse heads.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:02.640
And the enemies wouldn't be so bad if, like, the hitbox detection wasn't so weird.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:10.140
Yeah. I didn't have a hard time necessarily killing things, but I also had a hard time figuring out, like, what registers as a hit, what doesn't.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:15.140
Until Sean explained it just now, what registers as a hit on me even was, like, kind of confusing.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:23.540
There's no real auditory or visual feedback as to when you hit or when they hit unless, like, they just die.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.380
And, like, that even extends to when you game over.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.100
There's no, like, animation, like, immediately after you get hit, like, your final hit.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.340
It just cuts to black.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:36.660
And it could just be, like, wait, did I unplug the controller or something?

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:39.700
Power go out. It's, like, then there's an animation of her dropping down.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:44.520
I almost didn't want the animation, though, because for a minute, like, you know, because it is that long.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.420
It's, like, you know, the black stays on there for a second.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.020
I was, like, oh, she's dead.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:52.100
You know, like, I've completely lost consciousness.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:53.760
Like, she is dead.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:55.540
The screen is black.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.800
You've got to return the game, send it back.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.260
Like, I was, like, whoa. So that was pretty serious.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:04.940
Yeah. You also mentioned the upgrade system, Sean, with the different equipment and stuff.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.200
Now, SNK refers to these as RPG-like elements.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.420
What do you think of the upgrade system?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.740
I mean, it's 87.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:21.200
I guess you could, I mean, RPG-like elements is going to be used very sympathetically to a lot of these games.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.760
Like, yeah, it's an upgrade system.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.100
Yeah. Sure, it's an RPG-like element.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.560
It's just not an RPG element.

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.800
In the same way that, like, text in a box is an RPG-like element.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.220
Yeah. Yes. Or just, like, being a video game is an RPG-like element.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:43.680
I also didn't think it was, like, very helpful when, you know, like, if you pick up the sword, the flame sword, for instance, and then, like, another enemy drops the club.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.540
And it's, like, the game can't differentiate for you that, like, oh, you probably want to hold on to the flame sword.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:50.640
No, I'll go back to, like, the level one club.

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.800
Kind of like Ghost and Goblins where you've got to, like, avoid some of the drops.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:58.180
That isn't a problem unique to this game.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:01.720
Thankfully, they do despawn after a few seconds.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.600
But, yeah, it is still a problem.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:11.020
Don't you think it's weird, though, that, like, Super Mario Brothers solved this problem already for everybody and, like, no one's decided to take them up on it?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.640
No. No, I'm just saying, you know, think about it.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:16.820
It's, like, once you have the mushroom, right, you don't get offered the mushroom again.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:19.520
It's, like, going forward, you're going to get fire flowers, you know?

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:25.420
But they, I think the difference here is that, one, there are only two power-ups in Super Mario Brothers.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:29.600
That's true. A big flaw of the game.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:30.880
That is not a flaw.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.080
No, I'm joking. It was just, like, the way that we're talking.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:34.360
But there's only two.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.840
Like, it's, like, that was a big deal.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:41.440
And while, yeah, nobody wants the Red Billy Club again, even though it keeps dropping, there are...

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.740
Is that the official name? I don't know.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:43.840
No, I just like that. Probably.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:45.160
The Red Billy Club.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.520
I think that's what it's called in the manual, but I could be wrong.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:57.520
There are situations where you might want, like, the second weakest weapon, which is that hammer that just plows through the blocks a lot quicker.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:03.060
There are situations that you want these, but not all the time.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:06.800
So I think that it's a hard problem to solve.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:07.960
And that is not...

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.440
I mean, I fault this game for a lot, but that is not something I'm going to fault the game for.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.640
So, I mean, you know, there's eight worlds here.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.560
It's eight levels, really.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.200
It's not like there's multiple levels within the world.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.840
But, so, eight worlds.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:30.180
The world of forest, world of cave, world of sea, world of sky, world of ice, world of hell, world of labyrinth.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.960
I didn't think that labyrinth would come after hell.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:37.440
And then probably the best, like, final place ever.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.400
Like, the ultimate final destination.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:41.220
World of worlds.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.840
That is the final level.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.720
World eight is called the world of worlds.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:47.900
What does that look like?

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.120
What does the world of worlds look like?

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:52.180
The world of... I mean, like, I could pull something up for you, Joe.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.420
No, I mean, it's not just describable.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:55.700
Yeah, yeah. I guess, like...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.980
It's indescribable. Well, here's the thing.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:59.420
It's like, they did a nice touch with all these things.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.600
So I don't want to say world of worlds isn't looking cool.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:04.260
I actually didn't mind the graphical style.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:09.080
They did, like, at least a different enough looking thing where I was like, oh, this looks okay.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:12.720
It didn't look like... There were a couple times where I wasn't really sure what they were going for.

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:17.060
Right, but I guess what I mean is it didn't just look like generic NES looking stuff.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:22.220
It looked like they actually tried with the design of, like, even just the backgrounds, like, with the trees and stuff like that.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.540
It had, like, a little bit of a...

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.220
I don't want to say this.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:32.080
Like, I don't know. I don't want to say painted because it wasn't nice looking, but it definitely, like, looked more...

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:36.920
It had a style. Yes, an aesthetic to it that felt consistent across all the different worlds.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.100
Okay, I'll agree with that.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:42.540
So, you know, as I kind of said here, we had the world of sea and we'll have the world of sky, too.

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:47.240
Those things add more gameplay elements because in the world of sea, you kind of, like...

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.680
You turn into, like, a mermaid, right?

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:49.880
And you're swimming.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.280
And then in the world of sky, you also get wings.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.920
That's very chubby cherub-like.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:18:00.360
Like, did those things offer anything different enough for you guys to be like, hey, it's a whole different kind of game?

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:05.600
Or, like... They really only exist to get past very specific points in the level.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:17.240
I think there's a specific, very tight squeeze if you choose one route in the water level that you can't get through unless you're a mermaid.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:18.820
But that's about it.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:20.680
And you...

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.000
So, I'll be honest. I did not get to the world of sea.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.720
Okay. Um, you...

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:27.660
You don't keep the mermaid power indefinitely.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.000
You can lose the mermaid power up.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:29.980
You can lose it.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:33.140
In underwater? Yeah. I mean, you also don't carry it to the next level.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:34.760
Yeah, you definitely lose it there.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:38.200
And speaking of, like, just carrying things between levels, not...

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:44.760
The weirdest thing is how the transition between worlds works, where it's, like, cut to black, cut right to the next world.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.300
It's, like, there's no, like, real transition or anything.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.540
There's no... Well, here's the thing about, like, just the production of this game.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.480
Um, I...

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:58.240
They either didn't care or they were way too rushed because, yeah, you would expect some sort of transition between worlds.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:06.040
But let's just go back to the very first cutscene where she is in some brick building or this brick room.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:13.220
Yep. And she just jumps into the middle of the screen and immediately it starts to do this, like, weird psychedelic, like, spiral out to black.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:15.100
Almost a little Pokemon-ish.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:17.000
A little Pokemon-ish, but it has no...

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.040
That doesn't do...

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:18.940
It doesn't say anything.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:20.000
She's not doing anything.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:24.780
She just jumps and it cuts to black and then you go back to, like, the world of forest.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:31.000
In the arcade version I saw, there's a door there and that's the door of chaos.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.860
Yeah, the door that should not be opened.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:33.960
The door that shall not be opened.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.120
Yeah, and that's, like, the only thing that is part of the story.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.520
Exactly. Why bother?

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:45.940
Why not put the door there? Like, if you're not going to put any other cutscenes in this game and you still want to do the first one, like, why bother?

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.580
If you're not even going to put, like, a sprite in there for the door.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.680
Yeah. I agree with the abruptness of the whole game.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:20:01.980
Yeah. And then, like, you couple that with the lack of just enemy, you know, like, enemy variety but also just, like, the way that the enemies appear on the screen.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:09.140
Yeah. And one thing that we haven't talked about yet is that weird jump where, like, you press it once and it'll jump.

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:13.480
And then if you just time it right, maybe on the second jump, you'll jump, like, really far.

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:16.960
Yeah, to my experience, if you don't stop jumping, you'll continue jumping really high.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:20.080
But if you don't jump for, like, one second, you're jumping low again.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:27.100
And the low jump is effectively useless compared to the, like, you know, the game-breaking high jump.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:29.800
Yeah. Well, what do you mean by game-breaking?

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:33.220
Well, I don't mean, like, I guess I just mean, like, things that could have been in your way.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:36.640
Now you can just, like, jump right over them and onto the next platforms.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:43.500
And it seems like a really jinky way to do a, like, just to try and do, like, Super Mario.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.720
Like, why couldn't they do that?

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:47.600
Right. Like a memento.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.640
Like the run and jump kind of, yeah. Or just a hold button to go jumping higher.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.180
Like. No, yeah. That's true, too.

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:54.160
I don't know. Yeah.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.000
Yeah, yeah, yeah. That was weird because I thought that's what I was doing at first.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.280
It was like, oh, if you push down, like, really hard.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:02.540
Yeah. Yeah, and it's like, no, it doesn't register that stuff.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:08.600
All right. So after you get through all this stuff, the final boss is Dante, the guy who's, like, taking

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.280
over the fantasy world.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.360
And you fight him.

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:15.920
He's like a sphinx-looking creature, but stands.

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:17.260
Like a Cerberus.

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:19.620
Cerberus? Okay. Doesn't he have three heads?

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:20.940
A sphinx with three heads.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:22.860
That's pretty cool. But doesn't he have three heads?

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.360
I didn't, I didn't, to be honest, I looked at the picture very fast.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:30.220
But I'm pretty sure he has a sphinx-like feature to him.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:32.320
I don't think I would have made that up, but.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.380
I think our viewers think that we're making stuff up now.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:36.660
Okay, all right. So you're, you're good.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:37.980
Wait a minute. Is this Athena?

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:40.120
I'm talking about.

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:44.500
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Anyway, it doesn't really matter because the only point, the only reason why I'm bringing

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:48.840
up the final boss in the first place is that it's because it's possible to softlock yourself

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:54.860
out of the final boss by not picking up the necessary weapon, the bow that you need to

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:57.080
defeat Dante.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.560
And so you get to the end and it's like, if you didn't collect that bow, sorry kid, but

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.480
today's not your day with Athena.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:05.040
Start over.

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:07.560
He just, he's like impervious to everything else.

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:11.820
There's nothing that, like nothing tells you that.

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:15.960
There's no telegraphing that, hey, maybe pick up the bow.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:18.280
There's no lore.

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:19.940
If anything, the game is telegraphing.

00:22:20.260 --> 00:22:21.920
Try stuff. You know, like try out.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:23.240
No, no, no. I'm saying like try out everything.

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:26.600
Right. So like when you get the bow, it's like that should be the very last thing you pick up

00:22:26.600 --> 00:22:29.300
like mandatory item pick up and now you fight Dante.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:56.820
It's stupid. All right.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:01.760
So I'll take you through a couple of other things real fast.

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:07.540
So on the graphics, Toshiyuki and his 1996 interview had this to say.

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:11.280
In any event, I worked really hard on the graphics for Athena.

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:16.700
As you can imagine, now that our developments were more team-based, a healthy sense of competition

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:18.660
and rivalry developed between us.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:21.680
I didn't want to be the weakest link and slack off in my art.

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:24.360
I really gave the drawings my all on that game.

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:31.400
So just kind of, you know, enforcing that whole like crunch time momentum that we hear about

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:36.400
with even back then now in Japanese game culture is just like, you know, if you're not working

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:39.800
or if you're not working the hardest, you're seen as like the weakest link.

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:42.440
Yeah. It explains a lot.

00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:50.340
All right. And one other one on the fire sword, a little technical thing here that he got into.

00:23:50.340 --> 00:23:54.340
The biggest challenge during the creation of Athena was the fire sword.

00:23:54.560 --> 00:23:57.040
This humongous sword is one of Athena's weapons.

00:23:57.320 --> 00:24:02.020
During the initial planning, we thought it would look cool to have these big flames coming out of it.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:05.740
But due to hardware and memory limitations, we simply ran out of space.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:10.120
After countless revisions, we finally completed a usable fire sword effect.

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:14.860
And I know I'm patting myself on the back here, but I felt a huge surge of pride then.

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:20.520
Laughs. So here's something that I was just thinking of while I was listening to that.

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:26.340
And this sort of goes back to our shared experience as film students.

00:24:26.620 --> 00:24:33.660
Okay. I feel like this is when you're at, you're at like a forum where you're showing your films

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:37.900
and there's a Q&A portion and somebody asks you what was the biggest challenge.

00:24:39.300 --> 00:24:45.280
And they go into some very specific, like, oh, like this special effect just wasn't perfect.

00:24:45.300 --> 00:24:47.300
It took so hard to get that perfect.

00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:51.960
And then, but like this film that they're talking about, the sound sucked.

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:53.520
Like there's terrible acting.

00:24:53.660 --> 00:24:56.600
But like they're going on and on about this one special effect.

00:24:56.600 --> 00:24:58.440
It's like you're totally missing the point.

00:24:58.680 --> 00:25:00.540
You're focusing on the wrong thing. You're focusing on the wrong things.

00:25:00.720 --> 00:25:02.800
Like maybe get the general ideas right.

00:25:02.800 --> 00:25:07.320
And then imagine ending it too with like, but I did manage to get this special effect

00:25:07.320 --> 00:25:09.240
to work and I'm very proud of myself for that.

00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:14.260
Every single interview quote I've read from Toshi Yugi so far has been, listen to this,

00:25:14.360 --> 00:25:15.220
okay? On design.

00:25:15.940 --> 00:25:19.760
I, you know, I drew her myself on the fire sword.

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:23.840
I sound like I'm, I know I'm patting myself up on the back here, but I feel a huge surge

00:25:23.840 --> 00:25:25.540
of pride on the graphics.

00:25:25.580 --> 00:25:28.560
I didn't want to be the weakest link and slack off in my heart.

00:25:28.560 --> 00:25:33.400
I really gave my all for the drawings on this game and on the fan mail in an instant, all

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:35.600
the exhaustion and pain I felt dissipated.

00:25:35.940 --> 00:25:36.880
Wow. Okay.

00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:39.120
This guy has a Napoleon complex.

00:25:40.220 --> 00:25:42.660
And that is really funny.

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:44.400
I'm sure he's a nice guy.

00:25:44.500 --> 00:25:48.260
I think it's just really funny that we noticed that trend amongst him.

00:25:48.520 --> 00:25:52.020
And I do agree. This isn't a great game and he seems to really be hyped about it.

00:25:52.060 --> 00:25:54.640
And maybe like in Japan, it's a bigger deal.

00:25:54.640 --> 00:25:57.720
But in Western audiences, I feel like if you ask people about Athena.

00:25:57.720 --> 00:25:59.660
I mean, was it well received at the time?

00:25:59.780 --> 00:26:03.020
No. And that's the kind of like the weird thing is like a lot of people will tell you that

00:26:03.020 --> 00:26:06.980
Athena is one of the NES is like hardest games just because it's really hard to get

00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:08.480
through all eight levels.

00:26:08.500 --> 00:26:12.860
Like the idea of like you sitting down and being like, all right, I'm going to do this.

00:26:13.160 --> 00:26:14.980
You know, like nobody really says that about Athena.

00:26:15.180 --> 00:26:16.540
Ghosts and Goblins? Sure.

00:26:17.040 --> 00:26:20.560
Right. There's like enough substance to that game that you're like, I'm going to do this.

00:26:20.600 --> 00:26:22.380
And it sounds enjoyable to have that challenge.

00:26:22.600 --> 00:26:25.720
This challenge doesn't feel like it was designed to be a challenge.

00:26:26.280 --> 00:26:27.400
Exactly. It's not like you're playing the game.

00:26:27.400 --> 00:26:29.860
You're just fighting the software in a lot of parts of this.

00:26:30.020 --> 00:26:33.740
So I know you guys are now wondering what's next for Athena, right?

00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:35.220
Like what happens next?

00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:42.000
And I am glad to say that in 1993, a Japanese magazine interviewed SNK.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:44.860
We don't know who they interviewed from, but just an SNK representative.

00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:48.180
And they were just spitballing like, what do you think happened to Athena?

00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:50.540
So here's what SNK came up with on the spot.

00:26:51.300 --> 00:26:53.500
You can tell they never put any thought into this.

00:26:53.580 --> 00:27:00.540
So here we go. Having safely defeated the evil Emperor Dante of Fantasy World, Athena returns to the Kingdom

00:27:00.540 --> 00:27:03.260
of Victory and lives as a normal girl for a while.

00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:06.500
Her tomboyish nature, however, remains unchanged.

00:27:06.820 --> 00:27:11.200
And she has many adventures, the detail of which, due to a decree by the king restricting

00:27:11.200 --> 00:27:14.700
the dissemination of such information, I'm not at liberty to divulge.

00:27:14.700 --> 00:27:20.840
Eventually, she marries, has many children, and lives a blessed life of happiness and contentment.

00:27:21.060 --> 00:27:25.800
Her favorite magazine is Suteki na Okusan, the perfect wife.

00:27:26.380 --> 00:27:31.680
What? And she loves to sing Momo Yamaguchi at karaoke.

00:27:32.300 --> 00:27:37.880
The female descendants of the Asiama family also have ESP power.

00:27:38.720 --> 00:27:39.660
So this is...

00:27:39.660 --> 00:27:41.540
They just came up with that. That was just like an aside at the end?

00:27:41.580 --> 00:27:45.460
Just an aside. Like, all the future descendants have ESP power.

00:27:45.460 --> 00:27:46.960
You know what? I wanted...

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:47.960
A female have ESP power?

00:27:47.960 --> 00:27:49.740
I wanted to be like, you know what?

00:27:49.820 --> 00:27:51.040
Maybe they weren't like...

00:27:51.040 --> 00:27:55.000
Maybe she just happened to be a bored female character.

00:27:55.160 --> 00:27:58.320
It was a coincidence. But then they threw in that, like, the magazine.

00:27:58.820 --> 00:27:59.940
The perfect wife. And she got married.

00:27:59.940 --> 00:28:01.080
And she's like, she has many children.

00:28:01.320 --> 00:28:03.480
It's like, okay. She settled down and really...

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:06.200
Hold on. She doesn't need to be a warrior. I thought there was a sequel to this game.

00:28:06.560 --> 00:28:08.540
Okay, so I'll get into that next, Sean.

00:28:08.800 --> 00:28:12.420
I was kind of hoping we could do maybe the essential games list first.

00:28:14.660 --> 00:28:18.520
But since you bring it up, Sean, first, the bad news.

00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:21.520
Because, I mean, the arcade version is still bad.

00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:25.240
In this case, like, you know, like, I usually talk about, like, I played all the other versions.

00:28:25.240 --> 00:28:26.560
I tried all the other versions.

00:28:26.720 --> 00:28:27.980
They're all still bad, okay?

00:28:28.080 --> 00:28:33.580
Like, the arcade version is actually amazing how similar the NES version is to the arcade version.

00:28:35.220 --> 00:28:39.720
So, don't go out seeking a cabinet of the arcade version for this one.

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:45.140
So, sequels and spinoffs, I'm glad that you asked, Sean, because it's actually her descendant.

00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:46.540
Oh, one of those.

00:28:46.540 --> 00:28:49.840
Athena Asamiya from Psycho Soldier.

00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:53.920
Okay? And Psycho Soldier is a much more popular game that's recognizable.

00:28:54.820 --> 00:29:00.020
And I say much more popular, like, not that you should know it, but, like, way more popular than Athena.

00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:04.840
And that is, she is a main staple of the King of Fighters series.

00:29:05.240 --> 00:29:08.040
Oh. Athena Asamiya. I may have played her before.

00:29:08.300 --> 00:29:09.620
Yeah, she's the one dressed like the schoolgirl.

00:29:09.960 --> 00:29:11.180
Oh. Oh, that makes sense.

00:29:11.460 --> 00:29:13.200
Yeah. Purple hair.

00:29:13.240 --> 00:29:14.480
I just can't get it right with this kid.

00:29:14.640 --> 00:29:15.520
Yeah, purple hair.

00:29:15.860 --> 00:29:23.620
Anyway, the cool thing about this, now that we're going to talk about this before we get into the essential games list, is that I can tell you all about all the other things Athena's been doing, too.

00:29:23.620 --> 00:29:30.660
So outside of just having a descendant who's incredibly popular, Athena shows up as a secret boss in the SNK vs.

00:29:30.780 --> 00:29:32.740
Capcom SVC Chaos game.

00:29:33.200 --> 00:29:36.480
And so that's SNK and Capcom characters coming together.

00:29:36.760 --> 00:29:38.960
And there's two secret bosses.

00:29:38.960 --> 00:29:42.440
One, who you fight in hell, and it's the Red Devil.

00:29:42.940 --> 00:29:44.780
Of course. From Ghosts and Goblins.

00:29:45.560 --> 00:29:47.800
And then the other one. Let's bring the volcano back from Gradius, too.

00:29:48.560 --> 00:29:49.900
Upside down with the volcano.

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:51.240
Yeah. Anyway.

